    "explanation": "Movable type (US English; moveable type in British English) is the system and technology of printing and typography that uses movable components to reproduce the elements of a document. The mechanism involves separate pieces that stand for individual alphanumeric characters or punctuation marks; those pieces are used together to recreate the text of a document. Movable type is part of printing and typography practice and is typically used to put these character elements onto a medium, most often paper. By working at the level of individual characters and marks, movable type defines how text is composed and reproduced in printed form.",
